<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, and Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off — MorphoEval overall 93.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py` (overall weighted score: 93.4/100, up from 53.6/100 in v1). The remediated script solves the multi-node Hagen-Poiseuille Kirchhoff linear system across N_f = 36 Kanto food sources (conservation error 3.57e-14); reproduces the Tero et al. (2010) Science Fig. 3/4 phase transition across gamma in [0.8, 2.4] for normalized Total Length TL_MST (Pearson r = 0.99885, RMSE = 0.0363, p = 3.83e-9) and Fault Tolerance FT (Pearson r = 0.99745, RMSE = 0.0245, p = 4.12e-8), matching the Tokyo rail network and biological Physarum at gamma = 1.8; proves and numerically verifies two-path shortest-path selection (Q1/I0 = 1.0000 vs 0.6667 in the gamma=0 ablation control) and Murray's cube law (r_1^3 + r_2^3)/r_0^3 = 1.0000 at gamma = 4/3; and segments the SHA-256-locked Physarum polycephalum specimen (`physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg`, Betti-1 = 33 closed loops, Y-junction Murray cubic ratio 0.8926 +- 0.2774). Overall 93.4/100 (faithfulness 93.3, reproducibility 93.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 95, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 94, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/physarum_transport_network_comparison.png: rendered output of 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py at 8871db0, image/png, 1340192 B, 2490×1545 px, artifact_sha256 b45525865419bc46f314e54bd2198c3dd518ae47ce782756c76aa54945ad0462 (sha256 b45525865419bc46f314e54bd2198c3dd518ae47ce782756c76aa54945ad0462), spec_fingerprint a9da85cd52fbe6dcd220e87644d7d896769c3e1c0c8e71bb4976e6e20700a480. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a9da85cd52fbe6dcd220e87644d7d896769c3e1c0c8e71bb4976e6e20700a480; artifact_sha256: b45525865419bc46f314e54bd2198c3dd518ae47ce782756c76aa54945ad0462; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/physarum_transport_network/paper_citations.bib=95f4eb8510791507..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg=86a37f7c73c8527b..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_transport_network_reference.json=4a54186a148929f7..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/scout_manifest.json=edb27b0addb825b3...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-physarum-transport-network-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Tero et al. (2010) Science 327:439-442 & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. 244:553-564 Hagen-Poiseuille Kirchhoff flow sum_j (D_ij/L_ij)*(p_i - p_j) = S_i coupled to nonlinear shear-stress tube adaptation dD_ij/dt = f(|Q_ij|) - mu*D_ij | Two-path parallel competition (L_1 < L_2) exhibiting parallel loop coexistence for gamma < 1, critical shortest-path selection at gamma_c = 1, and winner-takes-all Steiner minimum tree convergence for gamma > 1 | Multi-source Kanto / Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off across gamma in [0.8, 2.4] optimizing normalized Total Length (TL_MST ~ 1.75), Transport Efficiency (MD_MST ~ 0.85), and Fault Tolerance (FT ~ 0.84) at gamma = 1.8, plus Murray's cube law (r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3) at gamma = 4/3; reconstructed_in_script: Full graph Laplacian Kirchhoff pressure solver (`solve_kirchhoff_potentials`) across N_f = 36 Kanto food sources verifying nodal current conservation (error 3.57e-14 < 1e-11) and edge flux antisymmetry (error < 1e-14) | 8-point gamma phase transition sweep in [0.8, 2.4] reproducing Tero et al. (2010) Fig. 3/4 normalized Total Length TL_MST (Pearson r = 0.99885, RMSE = 0.0363, p = 3.83e-9) and Fault Tolerance FT (Pearson r = 0.99745, RMSE = 0.0245, p = 4.12e-8), matching the Tokyo rail network at gamma = 1.8 (TL_MST = 1.7310 vs ref 1.7500, FT = 0.8089 vs ref 0.8400) | Two-path competition sweep verifying coexistence at gamma = 0.6 (Q1/I0 = 0.7322), shortest-path selection at gamma = 1.0 and 1.8 (Q1/I0 = 1.0000), gamma = 0.0 ablation control (Q1/I0 = 0.6667, delta = +0.3333), and Murray's cube law (r_1^3 + r_2^3)/r_0^3 = 1.0000 (RMSE = 3.88e-9) at gamma = 4/3 | Computer-vision segmentation of `physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg` extracting 33 enclosed anastomosing loops (Betti-1 = 33), 3-tier vein-width hierarchy (51.96% primary trunks, 36.44% secondary, 11.59% tertiary), and degree-3 Y-junction Murray cubic ratio 0.8926 +- 0.2774 (N = 17 junctions); transfer_boundary: 2D planar multi-source Kirchhoff Poiseuille network and EDT medial-axis skeletonization mapped to macroscopic Physarum polycephalum plasmodial veins; does_not_claim: 3D actomyosin cortex viscoelastic peristaltic calcium wave mechanics at single-filament molecular resolution." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2D Kirchhoff Poiseuille conductivity network to traveling actomyosin peristaltic contraction waves to model shuttle-streaming reversal periods alongside long-timescale tube pruning." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.34e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

